      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Churn rate by snapshot",
      "description": "Share of the models' population that churned in the 90 days after each snapshot. It swings with the season: customers who were active just before Christmas are the ones most likely to lapse afterwards. The axis starts at zero.",
